{"name":"Times Square Screens","hex":"#20c073","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"times","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of time","The circumstances of a certain time."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Multiplied by (see also 'ratio of comparison' sense at 'time')."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/times"},{"term":"square","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A polygon with four straight sides of equal length and four right angles; an equilateral rectangle; a regular quadrilateral.","Something characterized by a square, or nearly square, form.\nA cell in a grid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Shaped like a square (the polygon).","Forming a right angle (90°)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/square"},{"term":"screens","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of screen"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of screen"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/screens"}],"entries":[{"title":"Times Square","blocks":[{"text":"Times Square is one of the world's busiest pedestrian intersections, tourist destinations, and entertainment hubs. It is formed by the junction of Broadway, Seventh Avenue, and 42nd Street in Midtown Manhattan, New York City. Together with adjacent Duffy Square, Times Square is a bowtie-shaped plaza five blocks long between 42nd and 47th Streets. As an epicenter of the world's entertainment industry and as the physical hub of the Theater District, where most Broadway theaters are located, Times Square is constantly illuminated by numerous digital billboards and advertisements as well as businesses offering 24/7 service."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/New_york_times_square-terabass.jpg/330px-New_york_times_square-terabass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Times_Square","wikidata":"Q11259"},{"title":"Square","blocks":[{"text":"In geometry, a square is a regular quadrilateral. It has four straight sides of equal length and four equal angles. Squares are special cases of rectangles, which have four equal angles, and of rhombuses, which have four equal sides. As with all rectangles, a square's angles are right angles, making adjacent sides perpendicular. The area of a square is the side length multiplied by itself, and so in algebra, multiplying a number by itself is called squaring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg/330px-Square_with_offset_tick_marks.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square","wikidata":"Q164"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/1_times_square_night_2013.jpg/500px-1_times_square_night_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/1_times_square_night_2013.jpg/1280px-1_times_square_night_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/1_times_square_night_2013.jpg/500px-1_times_square_night_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1_times_square_night_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Longacre_Square%2C_New_York_City%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Longacre_Square%2C_New_York_City%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Longacre_Square%2C_New_York_City%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Longacre_Square%2C_New_York_City%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Broadway at 42nd Street in